# The engines the app has to run in. This replaces Angular's default ("baseline widely available",
# currently Chrome 119+ and Safari 17+) with a lower floor, so older phones keep working. The floor
# and the reasoning behind every line are in docs/architecture/frontend-architecture.md, "Supported
# browsers and WebViews". Change it together with that section, `minWebViewVersion` in
# capacitor.config.ts and the minimum OS versions in the native projects.
#
# Angular downlevels JavaScript syntax and CSS to these targets, but adds no polyfills for missing
# Web APIs - an API newer than this floor has to be feature-detected or polyfilled.
#
#   pnpm exec browserslist    lists what these queries select

# iOS: every browser engine on iOS is WebKit; WKWebView matches the iOS version, and the native
# minimum is 16.4 (IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET).
iOS >= 16.4
Safari >= 16.4

# Android: the System WebView is Chromium and updates through the Play Store independently of the
# OS. 108 is the first version with every layout feature the app relies on (`dvh`, container
# queries, `:has()`, cascade layers); Android 7 (API 24), the native minimum, gets up to 119.
Chrome >= 108
ChromeAndroid >= 108
Android >= 108
Edge >= 108

# The web demo on GitHub Pages only.
Firefox ESR
last 2 Firefox versions
